  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wetlands 4 Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A ten year global wetland ambition</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">At the global level, the programme promotes learning, knowledge exchange, and capacity building based on practical experiences from landscape initiatives. At the landscape level, W4R supports multi-stakeholder partnerships and on-the-ground restoration and livelihood activities in the Ziway&#x2013;Shalla sub-basin in Ethiopia, the Jeta-Pecixe-Cacheu landscape in Guinea-Bissau, and the Sundarbans in Bangladesh. Lessons from these landscapes&#x2014;together with experiences from long-term Wetlands International work in Indonesia and India&#x2014;are used to promote wider uptake of effective wetland restoration and resilience approaches.</narrative>
  </description>
